 "narration": [
  "The concrete under your feet already finished polluting. Before the building even opened.",
  "Cement and steel produce around fifteen percent of global CO2. Not construction emissions. All emissions.",
  "That's roughly seven times all of aviation, at about two percent.",
  "And it happens before day one. The building has spent a big chunk of its lifetime carbon just by existing as material.",
  "This is embodied carbon, and most net zero marketing leaves it out. Solar panels make a better photo than a spreadsheet about fly ash.",
  "The fix exists. Blended cements with fly ash or slag, mass timber where it fits, and recycled steel.",
  "Nobody in a finished lobby asks what the concrete used to be. Now you will."
 ],
